# =============================================================================
# Mint Shop UI — environment templates
# Copy to `.env` or `.env.local` and fill in values. Never commit real secrets.
# Restart `next dev` or redeploy after changes. NEXT_PUBLIC_* are baked in at build time.
# =============================================================================

# --- Shared: API (must include /api, no trailing slash on the base) ---
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.mint-shop.pro/api

# --- Shared: NextAuth secret (required). Generate: openssl rand -base64 32 ---
# AUTH_SECRET=
# Verbose auth logs in the Next.js terminal only (never in production): AUTH_DEBUG=1
# One-off diagnostics: random string; then GET /api/internal/auth-health?key=<same> (returns 404 if unset/wrong)
# AUTH_DIAG_SECRET=

# --- NextAuth session cookie (seconds). Default 365 days. Keycloak SSO must allow refresh that long — see API docs/KEYCLOAK.md ---
# AUTH_SESSION_MAX_AGE=31536000

# --- Keycloak (match your realm / client) ---
# KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_ID=mint-ecommerce
# KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET=
# KEYCLOAK_ISSUER=http://localhost:9091/realms/mint
# KEYCLOAK_ISSUER=https://auth.example.com/realms/mint

# =============================================================================
# PRODUCTION — multi-tenant *.yourdomain.com + single Keycloak callback on apex
# =============================================================================
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=https://api.mint-shop.pro/api
# AUTH_SECRET=<paste output of openssl rand -base64 32>
#
# Do NOT set NEXTAUTH_URL or AUTH_URL (breaks PKCE when users sign in on subdomains).
# The app syncs next-auth’s client base URL in Providers.tsx and rewrites localhost redirects
# in auth.ts using X-Forwarded-Host so sign-in never sends users to localhost in production.
# Never bake NEXTAUTH_URL=https://localhost:3000 into the production image or CI build env.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_MINT_ROOT_DOMAIN=mint-shop.pro
# AUTH_KEYCLOAK_REDIRECT_ORIGIN=https://mint-shop.pro
# AUTH_TRUST_HOST=true
#
# Keycloak client "Valid redirect URIs" must include exactly:
#   https://mint-shop.pro/api/auth/callback/keycloak
# (Optional for local testing against same client: http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/keycloak)
#
# Required for sign-in from *.mint-shop.pro when using AUTH_KEYCLOAK_REDIRECT_ORIGIN (PKCE cookies must span subdomain + apex):
# AUTH_COOKIE_DOMAIN=.mint-shop.pro

# =============================================================================
# LOCAL DEVELOPMENT — Keycloak on localhost or same issuer with localhost redirect
# =============================================================================
# NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api
# AUTH_SECRET=<same as above or another dev secret>
# NEXTAUTH_URL=http://localhost:3000
#
# Comment out or omit AUTH_KEYCLOAK_REDIRECT_ORIGIN so OAuth uses http://localhost:3000
# as redirect_uri. Otherwise Keycloak will send users to production apex.
#
# KEYCLOAK_ISSUER=http://localhost:9091/realms/mint
# KEYCLOAK_CLIENT_SECRET=<must match Keycloak confidential client, or empty if public>
#
# Keycloak "Valid redirect URIs" must include:
#   http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback/keycloak
